ce and intercultural exchange. Find out More Gilman Scholarship Opens the World to AU Students Life-changing global experiences that build career-ready confidence at AU. Find out More Events: Details & Registration Links Career Center Programs, Workshops & Events Fall 2026 programs, workshops, and events: Internship Insider | Tuesday, September 1, 2026 | 12 - 1 p.m. ET Considering Grad School? Start Here! | Wednesday, November 18, 2026 | 6 - 7 p.m. ET AU Ready (Internship) Pledge Information Session: Information Session #1 | Thursday, September 3, 2026 6:00 - 6:45 p.m. ET Information Session #2 | Monday, October 12, 2026 12:00 - 12:45 p.m. ET Information Session #3 | Monday, November 2, 2026 6:00 - 6:45 p.m. ET Information Session #4 | Thursday, December 10, 2026 12:00 - 12:45 p.m. ET Fall 2026 Job & Internship Fair and On-Campus Employment Fair Prep Events: Getting Your Resume Ready | September 8, 2026 | 6 –7 p.m. ET Fair Game – Your Guide to Success | September 9, 2026 | 6 –7 p.m. ET Crafting Your Elevator Pitch | September 10, 2026 | 12–1 p.m. ET Virtual Resume Stations | September 14, 2026 | 2–5 p.m. ET In-Person Resume Stations | September 15, 2026 | 1–4 p.m. ET Pre-Law Info Session: Applying to Law School | Wednesday, September 23, 2026 | 6 - 7 p.m. ET Considering Law School? | Wednesday, October 7, 2026 | 6 - 7 p.m. ET Career Foundations: Resumes + Cover Letters | Thursday, October 1, 2026 | 6 - 7 p.m. ET Personal Branding + Search Strategies | Tuesday, October 20, 2026 | 6 - 7 p.m. ET Networking + Informational Interviewing | Wednesday, October 28, 2026 | 6 - 7 p.m. ET Interviewing + Professionalism & Workplace Etiquette | Thursday, November 12, 2026 | 6 - 7 p.m. ET Download the Fall 2026 Educational Career Programs, Events & Networking Opportunities Guide - with links and full details. You can watch recordings of past workshops on our YouTube channel. Career Fairs and Networking Events Fall 2026 Career Fairs and Networking Events Info Sessions: Marriott International Employer Meet-Up | Monday, September 28, 2026 6 - 7 p.m. ET U.S. Intelligence Organization: Information Session | Tuesday, September 29, 2026 | 3:00 - 6 p.m. ET Job & Internship Fair AU’s Fall 2026 Job & Internship Fair and On-campus Employment (In-Person) Networking Opportunities Networking Reception Prep: Nonprofits Making a Difference | Tuesday, October 13, 2026 | 4:00 - 4:30 p.m. ET Nonprofits: Making a Difference Networking Reception | Tuesday, October 13, 2026 | 4:30 - 6:00 p.m. ET Networking Reception Prep: National Security & Intelligence Community | Tuesday, November 10, 2026 | 4:00 - 4:30 p.m. ET National Security & The Intelligence Community Networking Reception | Tuesday, November 10, 2026 | 4:30 - 6:00 p.m. ET Visit Handshake Events and filter for \"Career Fair\" under Category to find more . Coffee Chats with Employers & Alumni Meet 1:1 with employer representatives for learning and networking. Schedule your appointment and see who's coming through Handshake. View details about the Fall 2026 Coffee Chat schedule here . Spaces are limited. Slots open at 9 a.m. two weeks before the event. Please review our program policies and to learn how to sign up for these opportunities. Employer Meet-Ups & Webinars Connect with employers on-campus and virtually to learn about employment opportunities through these information sessions. Students can view upcoming Meet-Ups in Handshake . Events are updated daily. Previously Recorded Missed a webinar? Check out our YouTube channel for recordings. Here are some of our featured playlists: Career Readiness series - includes webinars on resumes and cover letters, networking, virtual interviewing and more. Hot Topics for Career Success - 5-10 minute videos on a variety of career topics. Peer Advisors Present - let our Peer Advisors guide you through Handshake, QuadJobs, and other Career Center resources. Schedule, Register, Explore Career Guides by Major Not sure what your career path might be, or how your major can help you get there? Use our career guides to explore the skills you'll develop through your coursework, how you can apply them in a variety of fields, and where to learn more about industries related to your major. Explore Career Guides Partner with Us! Students , if you would like to request a workshop for your organization or club, please read our expectations for student partnerships and then fill out this event request form . Faculty and staff , to learn more about how the AU Career Center can support or enhance your work explore the AU Career Center Faculty Quick Start Guide , or contact Emily Lelandais . Video - How to get to the AU Career Center Located on the 5th floor of the Butler Pavilion, our staff warmly welcomes students. Our commitment extends beyond just being a resource for perfecting resumes or interview practice; we strive to offer comprehensive guidance through every facet of the career journey. Video/Audio Descriptive Guide We often hear from our students about how helpful they find the guidance they receive at the AU Career Center. It is great having such a high-quality resource for our students. We have made it standard policy to urge our students to make appointments with you all. Philip Johnson, Chair of the Physics Department The advisor I spoke to was very understanding, encouraging, and open to discuss topics that I have been struggling with. They offered me impeccable guidance, providing numerous resources and advice to address the concerns I articulated throughout our meeting. Student, School of Public Affairs Very happy with the turnout and number of students who engaged with us. Majority of students approached us first which is much different than other schools. | This fair was a wonderful opportunity for the organization to get facetime with a multitude of students & candidates. Employers at our Fall Job & Internship Fair DISCOVER CAREER COMPETENCIES Being \"career ready\" means doing everything you can to prepare and execute a successful transition to the workplace. CAREER EXPLORATION & SELF-ASSESSMENTS Learn four career exploration steps and the self-assessments available to help you find your next steps. AI IN YOUR CAREER DEVELOPMENT Discover our latest advice on leveraging AI for career development. Keep in mind that our recommendations may change over time, and your usage may vary. AU ALUMNI NETWORK ON ALUMNIFIRE Connect with AU alumni for help with everything from general career advice to job opportunities. Sign up with your LinkedIn or Facebook account. AU EAGLES SOAR - FROM NEST TO THE NEXT The AU Career Center celebrates student success by highlighting recent and upcoming career experiences, including internships, research, volunteering, and other career-related activities. Complete the form and be featured in our Career Spotlights! FRAUDULENT JOBS AND INTERNSHIP POSTINGS Scammers are always looking for new ways to trick people. These scams can be difficult to detect. Sometimes scammers pose as employers and try to gain access to your bank account information or other personal information. 100 percent Student Satisfaction with Front Desk Services 98 percent Student Satisfaction with Career Advising 92 percent Positive Outcomes for May 2025 Graduates 4400 Massachusetts Avenue, NW Washington, DC 20016 (202) 885-1000 Contact Us Visit AU Work at AU Cookie Preferences Copyright © 2026 American University. Emergency Preparedness Policies Privacy Disclosure EEO Title IX Facebook Twitter Youtube LinkedIn Instagram Homepage loading By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Privacy Notice Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make 