      "description": "Careers | American University, Washington, DC Skip to main content Show Menu Search Search Website: Go Find People: Go Browse Departments & Services Log in myAU Portal Email Canvas Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Academics Academics Home Degrees Registration Schedule of Classes Study Abroad Summer Programs Online Programs Honors & Learning Communities Professional & Lifelong Learning Schools & Colleges College of Arts & Sciences Kogod School of Business School of Communication Baker School of Education School of International Service Professional Studies and Executive Education School of Public Affairs Washington College of Law Student Services Student Affairs Athletics Housing Dining & Retail New Students Career Services Student Organizations AU Arts Library Calendars Community Relations Alumni Give to AU Research About Show navigation Careers You are here: American University Human Resources Careers American University Careers Join us at American University and help us develop tomorrow's leaders who will change the world. Human Resources Home How We Work How AU Works Job Architecture FAQ Community Building Resources ADA & Workplace Reasonable Accommodations Out of State Employment Careers Careers Home Faculty Jobs Staff Jobs Search Jobs for Faculty, Staff & Students Student Jobs Current Faculty & Staff Faculty and Staff Tools & Resources Holidays Supervisor Resources Employment Verification Employee Relations New Hires Full-Time Faculty Full-Time Staff Adjunct Faculty Part-Time Staff Student Workers I-9 Verifications Benefits Professional Development Staff & Faculty Development Mentoring Matters Wellness & Work-Life AhealthyU Faculty & Staff Assistance Program Child Development Center Rooms for Nursing Parents Take Your Child to Work Day Community Compliance Employment Law & Posters Health & Welfare Notices Retirement Disclosures About HR Who to Contact in HR HR Department Listing American University Employees on Twitter on Twitter Back to top Employment Opportunities at American University We invite you to explore career opportunities at American University. At American University, we value open and honest inquiry, servant leadership, and the affirmation of the human dignity of all. We envision a thriving American University community where all individuals are understood, appreciated, and fully included, and where equal treatment, opportunities, and outcomes prevail. Our diverse community of students, faculty, and staff represent every state and more than 150 countries. Our internationally recognized faculty are today's thought leaders in the areas of public policy, law, the arts, communications, international development, and more. Our staff are innovative, service-oriented, and dedicated to moving the university towards achieving its strategic goals. We are committed to an excellent experience for all of our students, faculty and staff and share a passion for creating change through our knowledge and our work. American University offers a comprehensive benefits package including: Medical, dental, and vision plans Retirement plan with a generous 2:1 match on the first 5% Tuition remission Education benefits for dependent children Flexible Spending Accounts (FSA) Transit benefits Parental leave Short term medical leave Long term disability Back-up dependent care Pet insurance Group auto & home discounts We also provide a supportive environment that helps you to achieve a fulfilling work-life balance. Our dedicated staff at AhealthyU supports the health and well-being of AU faculty and staff through integrated programs, education and resources that encourage positive daily habits that fit your goals and lifestyle. These include a meditation series, cooking classes and fitness classes for both individuals and families. But what you won’t see elsewhere is a 100% retirement match, pet sitting, and on-campus tutoring. AU also offers college tuition for children after two years of employment and 20 credits per year for spouses or domestic partners after 4 months of employment. The Faculty Staff Assistance Program and our BHS Care program deliver professional counseling and mental health referral services for staff and their family members free of charge. Additionally, through our variety of Staff and Faculty Community Groups , employees can develop a deeper connection with the AU community and receive support from mentors, allies and peers. Our current Affinity Groups include: Asian American Native Hawaiian Pacific Islander Faculty & Staff Community Group Black Faculty & Staff Community Group Disability+ Faculty & Staff Community Group International Faculty & Staff Community Group Latino and Hispanic Faculty & Staff Community Group LGBTQ+ Faculty & Staff Community Group Military-Connected Faculty & Staff Community Group People of Color Faculty & Staff Community Group We are confident that you will find American University is a place to grow both personally and professionally and do meaningful work. American University is an E-Verify and Right to Work employer. Quick Links Search Faculty Openings Search Adjunct Openings Search Staff Openings Faculty Jobs Learn more about full-time and Adjunct Faculty positions. View Faculty Opportunities American University Ready Hire Are you looking for a full-time, part-time, or temporary administrative position? Explore if a Ready Hire position is right for you. Learn About Ready Hire Student Jobs View information about student jobs and internships. View Student Openings American Proud to be Tobacco and Smoke Free University Staff Jobs View a listing of full-time, part-time, and Ready Hire jobs. Learn About Staff Positions American University considers immigration sponsorship an important part of its efforts to recruit, hire, and retain a skilled work force with critical skills and knowledge. The U.S. Department of Labor requires employers seeking to employ an H1B worker to notify all employees at the same worksite that the University has filed a Labor Condition Application (LCA). You will find notices of LCA filing with the Employment and Training Administration, in accordance with 20 C.F.R. §655.734 on the myAU portal . Copies of the full LCAs will be available for public inspection at 3201 New Mexico Ave, N.W., Suite 270, Washington D.C. 20016. Complaints alleging misrepresentation of material facts on the LCA and/or failure to comply with the terms of the LCA may be filed with an office of the Wage and Hour Division of the United States Department of Labor. 4400 Massachusetts Avenue, NW Washington, DC 20016 (202) 885-1000 Contact Us Visit AU Work at AU Cookie Preferences Copyright © 2026 American University. Emergency Preparedness Policies Privacy Disclosure EEO Title IX Facebook Twitter Youtube LinkedIn Instagram Homepage By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Privacy Notice Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. More information Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always Active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only