    "https://www.american.edu/studentjobs/index.cfm": {
      "title": "Student Jobs",
      "description": "Student Jobs | American University, Washington, DC Skip to main content Show Menu Search Search Website: Go Find People: Go Browse Departments & Services Log in myAU Portal Email Canvas Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Academics Academics Home Degrees Registration Schedule of Classes Study Abroad Summer Programs Online Programs Honors & Learning Communities Professional & Lifelong Learning Schools & Colleges College of Arts & Sciences Kogod School of Business School of Communication Baker School of Education School of International Service Professional Studies and Executive Education School of Public Affairs Washington College of Law Student Services Student Affairs Athletics Housing Dining & Retail New Students Career Services Student Organizations AU Arts Library Calendars Community Relations Alumni Give to AU Research About Show navigation Student Jobs You are here: American University Student Jobs Career Center Home Frequently Asked Questions Federal Work Study AU Application Instructions Get Hired Get Paid CONTACT US AU Career Center 202-885-1804 careercenter@american.edu 4400 Massachusetts Avenue NW Washington, DC 20016 SPECIFIC DEPARTMENTS Off-Campus Employment AU Career Center careercenter@american.edu On-Campus Employment Office of Human Resources theworkline@american.edu Federal Work Study Financial Aid Office financialaid@american.edu Back to top On-Campus Student Jobs Discover and apply to on-campus, part-time student positions. Learn more Professional Jobs & Internships Access thousands of listings posted exclusively for students and alumni in Handshake. Log in to Handshake DC Reads Tutor and mentor K-8 youth in DC public schools. Apply to be a tutor Part-time jobs near campus Looking for a part-time job close to campus? Check out this Google map that shows employers near AU! See map Parker Dewey Gain professional experience with a micro-internship. Find opportunities Explore local part-time jobs and remote opportunities on Care.com and Taskrabbit *AU is not affiliated with these companies and is not responsible for the content or services provided by these websites. Care.com Taskrabbit AU’s Fall 2026 Job & Internship Fair + On-campus Employment AU’s Fall 2026 Job & Internship Fair will be held on Wednesday, September 16, 2026, from 1:00–4:00 p.m. ET in Bender Arena on the AU campus . This year, the On-campus Employment Fair will take place in conjunction with the Fall Job & Internship Fair , creating one convenient opportunity for students to explore a wide range of employment options in a single location. The On-campus Employment Fair will run from 1:00–3:30 p.m. ET and will feature on-campus part-time opportunities . Student registration opens on August 24, 2026 at 9:00am ET. Explore the employers attending this fall’s Job & Internship Fair + On-Campus Employment and use the filterable tags to search by industry, job type, or other criteria that matter to you. ON-CAMPUS UNITS: The Fall 2026 On-Campus Employment Fair provides an opportunity for on-campus departments (hiring both Federal Work-Study–eligible and non-FWS positions) recruiting for paid part-time roles to connect with students seeking employment during the semester. Employer registration for on campus units is FREE for the Fair! If you are interested in participating, please register your office or unit. Registration opens June 8 and closes August 31, or earlier if capacity is reached. REGISTER HERE for the Fall 2026 On-Campus Employment. Registrations will be reviewed and, where appropriate, related offices and units will be grouped into shared hiring hubs. Space is limited, and tables will be assigned on a first-come, first-served basis. If all tables are reserved, a waitlist will be created in order of registration. If you have any questions, please contact the event lead, Julie Jones, at juliej@american.edu . Event co-sponsored by the AU Career Center, the Office of Human Resources, the Student Affairs, and the Office of Financial Aid Need help before applying? Set up an appointment with a career advisor, practice interviewing , read up on resumes , or check out our professional image guide . International students at AU must visit the International Student and Scholar Office as the first step in their job search process. Staff and Faculty Hiring Students Need help posting your position for students? Please contact the Human Resources representative in your unit. For immediate assistance reach out to TheWorkLine@american.edu How to Find Part-time Employment Looking for a Part-Time Job This Fall? Explore Our Fall 2026 Employment resource on finding local paid, part-time, and temporary jobs that fit a student’s class and campus schedule. After You're Hired Important Steps Before You Begin Working Once you've been hired for a student employment position, you'll need to complete several required tasks before your first day. Download the guide that covers the hiring process, required employment forms, Federal Work Study information, guidance for international students, and key contacts to help you get started successfully. Scam alert Recently, two scams have been making their way around the AU community, sent from compromised AU email addresses that fraudulently claim to offer an internship opportunity at UNICEF or a part-time job at Samaritan's Purse. See our tips to avoid scams. 4400 Massachusetts Avenue, NW Washington, DC 20016 (202) 885-1000 Contact Us Visit AU Work at AU Cookie Preferences Copyright © 2026 American University. Emergency Preparedness Policies Privacy Disclosure EEO Title IX Facebook Twitter Youtube LinkedIn Instagram Homepage By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. Privacy Notice Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. More information Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always Active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable information. Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. All information these cookies collect is aggregated and therefore anonymous. If you do not allow these cookies we will not know when you have visited our site, and will not be able to monitor its performance. Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies